            <ArticleTitle>Thoracic Sympathectomy for Severe Refractory Multivessel Coronary Artery Spasm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>159-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.amjcard.2015.10.018</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0002-9149(15)02097-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery spasm is a rare but potentially fatal disease. Herein, we report a case of recurrent ST-segment myocardial infarctions and ventricular fibrillation complicating severe multivessel coronary artery spasm successfully treated with bilateral thoracic surgical sympathectomy.</AbstractText>
